<title>USA: St. Paul Bancorp extends stock buyback.</title>
<headline>St. Paul Bancorp extends stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>St. Paul Bancorp Inc said Wednesday its board had extended for six months its stock repurchase program.</p>
<p>Of the 1.125 million shares authorized to be repurchased under the program -- or roughly five percent of outstanding shares -- 168,750 were purchased during the last six months at an average price of $22.46 a share, it said.</p>
<p>Amounts have been restated to reflect a recent five-for-four stock split.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
